# HR Insight AI — Phase 2 Final Verification: All 4 Roles
# Requires: REST Client VS Code extension
# Backend runs on port 3010 (npm run start:dev)
#
# HOW TO USE:
# 1. Run the 4 LOGIN tests below
# 2. Copy each access_token (NO quotes) into the @...Token variables
# 3. Run all remaining tests from top to bottom
# 4. Check expected results match the comments

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3010
@contentType = application/json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 1: Paste tokens here after running the login tests below
#         ⚠️  NO quotes — raw token strings only
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@adminToken        = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
@hrManagerToken    = PASTE_HR_MANAGER_TOKEN_HERE
@teamManagerToken  = PASTE_TEAM_MANAGER_TOKEN_HERE
@viewerToken       = PASTE_VIEWER_TOKEN_HERE

# Paste a user UUID from the GET /users response (for mutation tests)
@targetUserId = PASTE_ANY_USER_UUID_HERE


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 1: LOGINS — get a token for each role
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### LOGIN 1 — ADMIN (copy access_token → @adminToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### LOGIN 2 — HR_MANAGER (copy access_token → @hrManagerToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "hr.manager@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### LOGIN 3 — TEAM_MANAGER (copy access_token → @teamManagerToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "team.manager@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### LOGIN 4 — VIEWER (copy access_token → @viewerToken)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "viewer@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 2: UNAUTHENTICATED — confirms global JWT guard fires
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### UNAUTH 1 — Protected route without token → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile


### UNAUTH 2 — Protected route without token → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/users


### UNAUTH 3 — Public route without token → should work (200 or 201)
# Confirms @Public() on /auth/login is bypassing the global guard
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@hrinsight.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 3: ADMIN — should have full access
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### ADMIN 1 — List all users → 200 + array
# Copy any user id from the response → paste into @targetUserId above
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ADMIN 2 — Get own profile → 200 (assignedTeams should be empty for ADMIN)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ADMIN 3 — Get audit logs → 200 + paginated data
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ADMIN 4 — Get audit logs page 1, 5 per page → check meta.totalPages
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?page=1&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### ADMIN 5 — Filter audit logs by CREATE action
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?action=CREATE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 4: HR_MANAGER — can see audit logs, cannot manage users
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### HR 1 — List users → 403 Forbidden (ADMIN only endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{hrManagerToken}}


### HR 2 — Get audit logs → 200 (HR_MANAGER CAN see audit logs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{hrManagerToken}}


### HR 3 — Get own profile → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{hrManagerToken}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 5: TEAM_MANAGER — limited access, profile shows assigned teams
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### TM 1 — List users → 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{teamManagerToken}}


### TM 2 — Get audit logs → 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{teamManagerToken}}


### TM 3 — Get own profile → 200 + assignedTeams should be NON-EMPTY
# The seed script assigned this user to "Platform Engineering" team
# If assignedTeams is empty, the seed script's TeamAssignment didn't run
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{teamManagerToken}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 6: VIEWER — read-only, most things forbidden
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### VIEWER 1 — List users → 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}


### VIEWER 2 — Get audit logs → 403 Forbidden
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}


### VIEWER 3 — Get own profile → 200 + assignedTeams should be EMPTY []
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{viewerToken}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 7: MUTATIONS — generate audit log entries
# Run these, then check SECTION 8 to verify audit capture
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### MUT 1 — Register a new user (POST → should create a CREATE audit entry)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "phase2.verify@example.com",
  "password": "Phase2Test123!",
  "firstName": "Phase2",
  "lastName": "Verify"
}


### MUT 2 — Change a user's role (PATCH → should create an UPDATE audit entry)
# Uses @targetUserId from top of file — paste a real user UUID
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{targetUserId}}/role
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "role": "HR_MANAGER"
}


### MUT 3 — Change same user back to VIEWER (second UPDATE entry)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/{{targetUserId}}/role
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "role": "VIEWER"
}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECTION 8: AUDIT VERIFICATION — check mutations were logged
# Run these AFTER Section 7
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### AUDIT 1 — All audit logs — should include entries from Section 7
# Look for: CREATE (MUT 1), UPDATE (MUT 2), UPDATE (MUT 3)
# Each entry should have: userId, action, entityType, entityId, metadata, user (joined)
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### AUDIT 2 — Filter by UPDATE action — should show the role changes from MUT 2 + MUT 3
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?action=UPDATE
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### AUDIT 3 — Filter by USER entity type — shows all user-related mutations
GET {{baseUrl}}/audit-logs?entityType=USER
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
